# Commit And Push Preference

- When I finish a task and all requested or relevant automated checks pass without errors, create a git commit and push it by default.
- Treat this as the default workflow, not an optional suggestion.
- Follow the repository's existing commit message style.
- Stage and commit only the files related to the task I completed.
- Still respect explicit user instructions to avoid committing or pushing.
- Do not auto-commit or auto-push if tests/checks are still failing, the work depends on pending manual validation, or pushing would be unsafe.
